WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:03.333
You've checked the fence, the chain
and the actions only people take.

00:00:03.333 --> 00:00:05.000
Now run it in minutes a day.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.300
Start every morning knowing the one
move, and know what each action cost,

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.567
down to the single run.

00:00:09.633 --> 00:00:12.500
By the end you'll have a
morning loop and a weekly one.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:15.033
Mornings: Mission Control,
the queue, the Hot list.

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:16.933
Weeks: the engine pages
and the cost ledger.

00:00:16.967 --> 00:00:19.033
Mia starts Monday with ten tabs open,

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:20.833
trying to learn what the
system did overnight.

00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:23.667
The bill, when it comes, is
one number nobody can explain.

00:00:23.733 --> 00:00:26.567
First, Mission Control, pinned
at the top of the left rail.

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:30.233
At the top is today's one move: the
oldest approval waiting on a person,

00:00:30.233 --> 00:00:32.300
with one click to approve
if you're the right person.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:35.067
Under it sit tiles for qualified
coverage, open pipeline,

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:37.733
reply rate and spend, then
ranked risks from your monitors.

00:00:37.733 --> 00:00:40.967
A tile with no published metric
shows a dash, never a made up number.

00:00:40.967 --> 00:00:43.033
Or ask your agent: "Brief me on today".

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:44.633
It isn't the same page for everyone.

00:00:44.633 --> 00:00:46.800
Each role profile has
its own seat dashboard.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.800
Profiles only narrow what a person can do,

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:51.000
and a member's agents
inherit the same limits.

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:55.433
Leo reads the overnight log first:
scores refreshed, drafts made, syncs run.

00:00:55.433 --> 00:00:58.067
A failed line opens its run,
with the step by step journal,

00:00:58.067 --> 00:00:59.233
so he lands on the cause.

00:00:59.233 --> 00:01:02.900
In the console: Mission Control, then
Operate, Runs. Or ask your agent.

00:01:02.933 --> 00:01:05.533
Second, the Focus queue, for
when one move isn't enough.

00:01:05.533 --> 00:01:07.467
In the console: Operate, Needs a human.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.267
It lists only what
still waits on a person,

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:12.600
and opening one shows the frozen
payload as a diff. Or ask your agent.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.600
It can brief you, but deciding is yours.

00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:17.067
Third, the Hot list. In
the console: CRM, Hot list.

00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:18.367
Accounts are ranked by their latest score,

00:01:18.367 --> 00:01:22.567
with the live signals behind them.
Open the why drawer on the top account.

00:01:22.567 --> 00:01:25.867
It shows the reasons, the caps
and negatives that held it back,

00:01:25.867 --> 00:01:28.033
how old signals decayed,
and the buying committee.

00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:30.867
If the ranking looks wrong, Mia
flags the score from the lead queue,

00:01:30.867 --> 00:01:31.800
and that feeds tuning.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:34.833
Or ask your agent: "Show the hot
list and why number one is hot".

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:39.200
Fourth, each engine page opens on
an overview: Dry or Live, its KPIs,

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:42.933
what it needs, approvals waiting,
recent actions with undo,

00:01:42.933 --> 00:01:46.567
and the definitions it runs on. Read
the engine you changed last week first.

00:01:46.567 --> 00:01:50.300
In the console: Engines, then
the engine. Or ask your agent.

00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:53.333
Fifth, the daily update, the same
morning read delivered to you:

00:01:53.333 --> 00:01:56.467
what was done yesterday, what waits
on a human, numbered open questions,

00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:59.900
and sync health. In the console:
Operate, Daily update. Or ask your agent.

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:02.833
Each person opts in to delivery,
owners and admins set the hour,

00:02:02.833 --> 00:02:04.700
and an AI summary is always labelled.

00:02:04.733 --> 00:02:06.533
The bell holds your notifications.

00:02:06.533 --> 00:02:08.267
The Waiting on you badge adds the open

00:02:08.267 --> 00:02:10.267
asks you own to the
approvals that need you,

00:02:10.267 --> 00:02:11.867
so there's one number to clear.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:13.900
On the home page sits the first win card.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.633
Each milestone is computed from
real facts, never ticked by hand,

00:02:16.633 --> 00:02:19.733
and a fact that can't be read
shows unknown with its reason.

00:02:19.733 --> 00:02:21.433
Or ask your agent for your next step.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:22.767
Nudges are the reminders.

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:25.967
While setup is unfinished, owners
and admins see one in the app first.

00:02:25.967 --> 00:02:27.833
Email is opt in, at most once a week,

00:02:27.833 --> 00:02:29.567
with an unsubscribe link in every mail.

00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:32.867
If email isn't configured, the nudge
says so. An agent can't turn it on.

00:02:32.933 --> 00:02:35.300
Now the other half of the
rhythm: what it costs.

00:02:35.333 --> 00:02:37.967
In the console: Operate,
Cost, the cost ledger.

00:02:37.967 --> 00:02:40.400
It's double entry: money
is reserved before a call,

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.933
settled when it finishes,
or released if it never ran.

00:02:42.933 --> 00:02:44.900
Released reservations
don't count as spend.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:46.800
Every line links to the run that spent it.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:50.267
Or ask your agent: "What did we spend
this week, and which runs spent it".

00:02:50.333 --> 00:02:53.567
Three kinds of money move: model
calls, data lookups like enrichment,

00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:56.700
and ad spend. The first two are booked
to the play or run that caused them.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:59.733
That turns a monthly bill into a
decision: this play cost this much,

00:02:59.733 --> 00:03:01.200
and here's what it was credited with.

00:03:01.267 --> 00:03:03.200
Spend has ceilings at several levels.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:06.067
Above the per call cap on data
lookups, a person approves.

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:09.733
When a budget by organization, environment, agent or play would be exceeded,

00:03:09.733 --> 00:03:12.300
the action doesn't quietly run
or vanish. It becomes a proposal.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.167
Enrichment has a monthly cap too,

00:03:14.167 --> 00:03:16.600
and enriches your best accounts
first when money is short.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:20.467
In the console: Operate, Cost for the
lines, and Settings, Safety for usage.

00:03:20.467 --> 00:03:21.500
Or ask your agent.

00:03:21.533 --> 00:03:25.567
To judge a play, open Engines,
Plays, Results: runs, outcomes,

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:29.000
credited revenue and spend,
side by side. Or ask your agent.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:33.333
Syncing the same ad window again
updates rows instead of adding them,

00:03:33.333 --> 00:03:34.900
so spend never double counts.

00:03:34.967 --> 00:03:38.467
Pro move: set conservative caps in
week one, while you're in Dry Mode.

00:03:38.467 --> 00:03:41.333
After a week of real ledger lines
you know what a normal day costs.

00:03:41.333 --> 00:03:43.900
Tighten the caps to that,
then widen on purpose,

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:45.500
with a person approving each change.

00:03:45.567 --> 00:03:48.933
The objection: a dashboard I
can't trust is worse than none.

00:03:48.933 --> 00:03:50.500
A tile with no published
metric shows a dash.

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:53.300
The first win is computed from real facts,

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.233
and says unknown when it can't read one.

00:03:55.233 --> 00:03:57.400
And the ledger counts
only money that settled.

00:03:57.433 --> 00:04:00.567
That was Mia's Monday: one approval
decided, one score flagged,

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:02.400
one update read, one cap checked.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:05.933
A short morning, and she knows what
the system did and what it cost.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:09.233
You run this in minutes, and you
can explain every line of spend.

00:04:09.233 --> 00:04:12.000
Open Mission Control tomorrow
and clear the one move.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.700
Next is Environments: dev,
staging and production.
